IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 57: PERSONAL DATA PROTECTION ACT 2012 (13 rules): registering the Personal Data Protection
-- Commission's Directions and Notices, and an Appeal Committee's Decisions, in the District Court.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  A MAYBE BOOLEAN answer is:
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (the FALSE-kind comment quotes them).
--   NOTHING     the text does not answer on these facts (the NOTHING-kind comment says why).
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- O 3 r 2(1) is a caveat on every answer: every requirement in the Rules is subject to the Court's
-- discretion to order otherwise in the interests of justice; it is not threaded as an input.
-- What follows non-compliance with a Rule is O 3 r 2(4) (the Court "may" waive it, reject the document,
-- dismiss, and so on); the functions below that say NOTHING for a "must" not done cite that provision.
--
-- BORROWED FACTS.  The Personal Data Protection Act 2012 is not among the sources.  Its sections
-- (48H, 48I, 48J, 48K, 48L, 48M, 48N, 48O, 48P, 48Q, 48R) are named in the inputs and asked as facts.
--
-- TIME.  O 3 r 3(1) says the Interpretation Act does not apply to the calculation of time in these
-- Rules, so no Interpretation Act module is used.  Each period is a `Period` constant named for its
-- rule; whether an act was in time is a comparison with the input `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the
-- act` (seam S-T1: roc1's O 3 r 3 computes it, and the merged file wires it).
-- Judgment calls QA to QE are tagged "QX:" in comments; work/forks.py lists them for the fork register.

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 57 -- Personal Data Protection Act 2012`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- definitions of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 57 r 1 defined term` IS ONE OF
    `o 57 r 1 Act`
    `o 57 r 1 Appeal Committee`
    `o 57 r 1 Commission`

-- What a defined term means, as the Rule states it, and what it points at.
DECLARE `o 57 r 1 meaning` HAS
    `o 57 r 1 the term` IS A STRING
    `o 57 r 1 means` IS A STRING
    `o 57 r 1 points at` IS A STRING

-- src:6799 | 1. In this Order — “Act” means the Personal Data Protection Act 2012, and any reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act;
-- src:6800 | “Appeal Committee” means a Data Protection Appeal Committee nominated under section 48P(4);
-- src:6801 | “Commission” means the Personal Data Protection Commission established by section 5.
@ref O 57 r 1 (src:6799-6801)
GIVEN term IS A `o 57 r 1 defined term`
GIVETH A `o 57 r 1 meaning`
`o 57 r 1 the meaning of the defined term` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `o 57 r 1 Act` THEN `o 57 r 1 meaning` OF "Act", "the Personal Data Protection Act 2012", "the Personal Data Protection Act 2012"
    WHEN `o 57 r 1 Appeal Committee` THEN `o 57 r 1 meaning` OF "Appeal Committee", "a Data Protection Appeal Committee nominated under section 48P(4)", "section 48P(4) of the Act"
    WHEN `o 57 r 1 Commission` THEN `o 57 r 1 meaning` OF "Commission", "the Personal Data Protection Commission established by section 5", "section 5 of the Act"

-- "any reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act".  The text carves out no
-- reference that names another Act expressly; it is silent on one.
-- src:6799 | 1. In this Order — “Act” means the Personal Data Protection Act 2012, and any reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act;
@ref O 57 r 1 (src:6799)
GIVEN `the reference is to a section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference names another Act expressly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 1 a reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the reference names another Act expressly`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Rule does not say what a reference does that names another Act
        IF `the reference is to a section`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any reference to a section" speaks only of a reference to a section

-- Membership of the defined terms.  Both definitions say "means", so a body that does not fit is outside the term and the text says no in
-- its own words (JUST FALSE).  A definition that only said "includes" would answer NOTHING for a thing it does not name; neither of these does.
-- The term "Act" is not given a membership function: "means the Personal Data Protection Act 2012" has one fact to ask, whether the statute
-- is that Act, and the meaning string above already states it.
-- src:6800 | “Appeal Committee” means a Data Protection Appeal Committee nominated under section 48P(4);
@ref O 57 r 1 (src:6800)
GIVEN `the panel is a Data Protection Appeal Committee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the panel was nominated under section 48P(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 1 the panel is an Appeal Committee` MEANS
    IF `the panel is a Data Protection Appeal Committee` AND `the panel was nominated under section 48P(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a Data Protection Appeal Committee nominated under section 48P(4)"

-- src:6801 | “Commission” means the Personal Data Protection Commission established by section 5.
@ref O 57 r 1 (src:6801)
GIVEN `the body is the Personal Data Protection Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the one established by section 5 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 1 the body is the Commission` MEANS
    IF `the body is the Personal Data Protection Commission` AND `the body is the one established by section 5 of the Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means the Personal Data Protection Commission established by section 5"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2 -- powers under section 48M exercisable by Judge or Registrar`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6803 | 2. —(1) Subject to paragraph (2), the powers conferred on the District Court by section 48M may be exercised by a District Judge in chambers or the Registrar. (2) The powers conferred on the District Court by section 48M(4) may only be exercised by a District Judge.
@ref O 57 r 2(1) (src:6803)
GIVEN `the power is the one conferred by section 48M(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `Decision maker`
      `the District Judge sits in chambers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 2(1) the power under section 48M may be exercised by the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the power is the one conferred by section 48M(4)`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to paragraph (2)": paragraph (1) does not grant the powers of section 48M(4), which paragraph (2) governs
        IF person EQUALS `A District Judge` AND `the District Judge sits in chambers`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF person EQUALS `The Registrar`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be exercised by a District Judge in chambers or the Registrar" grants the powers to those two and says nothing of anyone else

-- src:6803 | 2. —(1) Subject to paragraph (2), the powers conferred on the District Court by section 48M may be exercised by a District Judge in chambers or the Registrar. (2) The powers conferred on the District Court by section 48M(4) may only be exercised by a District Judge.
@ref O 57 r 2(2) (src:6803)
GIVEN `the power is the one conferred by section 48M(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `Decision maker`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 2(2) the power under section 48M(4) may be exercised by the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the power is the one conferred by section 48M(4)`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (2) speaks only of "the powers conferred on the District Court by section 48M(4)"
        IF person EQUALS `A District Judge`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may only be exercised by a District Judge"

-- Paragraphs (1) and (2) gathered by hand (option B of ruling E1, guidance for hand-gathering only).
GIVEN `the power is the one conferred by section 48M(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `Decision maker`
      `the District Judge sits in chambers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 2 the power under section 48M may be exercised by the person` MEANS
    IF `the power is the one conferred by section 48M(4)`
    THEN `o 57 r 2(2) the power under section 48M(4) may be exercised by the person` `the power is the one conferred by section 48M(4)` person
    ELSE `o 57 r 2(1) the power under section 48M may be exercised by the person` `the power is the one conferred by section 48M(4)` person `the District Judge sits in chambers`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 3 -- application to register a Direction, Notice or Decision`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 57 r 3 who made the instrument` IS ONE OF
    `o 57 r 3 the Commission`
    `o 57 r 3 an Appeal Committee`
    `o 57 r 3 someone else`

-- The provision of the Personal Data Protection Act 2012 under which the instrument was made,
-- as rule 3 names them.
DECLARE `o 57 r 3 provision it was made under` IS ONE OF
    `o 57 r 3 section 48H(2)`
    `o 57 r 3 section 48I`
    `o 57 r 3 section 48L(4)`
    `o 57 r 3 section 48N(6)(b)(i)`
    `o 57 r 3 section 48Q(5)`
    `o 57 r 3 another provision`

-- An instrument as a person who holds it can describe it.
DECLARE `o 57 r 3 instrument` HAS
    `o 57 r 3 made by` IS A `o 57 r 3 who made the instrument`
    `o 57 r 3 made under` IS A `o 57 r 3 provision it was made under`
    `o 57 r 3 is a direction or a decision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 57 r 3 is a written notice for the payment of a sum` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 57 r 3 the sum includes a financial penalty imposed under section 48J(1), or varied under section 48N(6)(b)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 57 r 3 the sum includes the interest payable under section 48K(10) on that penalty` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:6805 | 3. An application to register in the District Court — ( a )
-- src:6806 | any direction made by the Commission under section 48H(2), 48I or 48L(4), including any direction varied by the Commission under section 48N(6)( b )(i) (called in this Order a Direction);
@ref O 57 r 3(a) (src:6805-6806)
GIVEN instrument IS A `o 57 r 3 instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 3(a) the instrument is a Direction` MEANS
    IF    instrument's `o 57 r 3 made by` EQUALS `o 57 r 3 the Commission`
      AND instrument's `o 57 r 3 is a direction or a decision`
      AND (   instrument's `o 57 r 3 made under` EQUALS `o 57 r 3 section 48H(2)`
           OR instrument's `o 57 r 3 made under` EQUALS `o 57 r 3 section 48I`
           OR instrument's `o 57 r 3 made under` EQUALS `o 57 r 3 section 48L(4)`
           OR instrument's `o 57 r 3 made under` EQUALS `o 57 r 3 section 48N(6)(b)(i)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "(called in this Order a Direction)" names the listed directions; it does not say that no other instrument is a Direction; FORK: NOTHING, because the parenthesis gives the class a name and carries neither "means" nor "only", the words that make a definition say no in its own words / other: JUST FALSE, because the parenthesis is the definition of the term and an instrument outside its description is not a Direction in this Order (the same question arises wherever a rule says "(called ...)")

-- src:6807 | ( b )
-- src:6808 | any written notice by the Commission (called in this Order a Notice) for the payment of any sum comprising — (i)
-- src:6809 | a financial penalty imposed under section 48J(1), including a financial penalty varied by the Commission under section 48N(6)( b )(ii); and
-- src:6810 | (ii)
-- src:6811 | any interest payable under section 48K(10) on that financial penalty; or
@ref O 57 r 3(b) (src:6807-6811)
GIVEN instrument IS A `o 57 r 3 instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 3(b) the instrument is a Notice` MEANS
    IF    instrument's `o 57 r 3 made by` EQUALS `o 57 r 3 the Commission`
      AND instrument's `o 57 r 3 is a written notice for the payment of a sum`
      AND instrument's `o 57 r 3 the sum includes a financial penalty imposed under section 48J(1), or varied under section 48N(6)(b)(ii)`
      AND instrument's `o 57 r 3 the sum includes the interest payable under section 48K(10) on that penalty`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "(called in this Order a Notice)" names a sum comprising a penalty "and" the interest on it; a notice for the penalty alone is neither said to be a Notice nor said not to be; FORK: NOTHING, as for a Direction, because "called" is neither "means" nor "only" / other: JUST FALSE, because the parenthesis defines the term, so a notice outside the description (a penalty alone, or a notice by someone else) is not a Notice in this Order

-- src:6812 | ( c )
-- src:6813 | any direction or decision made by an Appeal Committee under section 48Q(5) (called in this Order a Decision),
@ref O 57 r 3(c) (src:6812-6813)
GIVEN instrument IS A `o 57 r 3 instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 3(c) the instrument is a Decision` MEANS
    IF    instrument's `o 57 r 3 made by` EQUALS `o 57 r 3 an Appeal Committee`
      AND instrument's `o 57 r 3 is a direction or a decision`
      AND instrument's `o 57 r 3 made under` EQUALS `o 57 r 3 section 48Q(5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "(called in this Order a Decision)" names the listed directions and decisions; it does not say that no other instrument is a Decision; FORK: NOTHING, as for a Direction, because "called" is neither "means" nor "only" / other: JUST FALSE, because the parenthesis defines the term, so an instrument outside the description is not a Decision in this Order

-- The scope of rule 3: the application is for a Direction, a Notice or a Decision.
GIVEN instrument IS A `o 57 r 3 instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 3 the instrument is a Direction, a Notice or a Decision` MEANS
        `o 57 r 3(a) the instrument is a Direction` instrument EQUALS JUST TRUE
    OR `o 57 r 3(b) the instrument is a Notice` instrument EQUALS JUST TRUE
    OR `o 57 r 3(c) the instrument is a Decision` instrument EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- src:6805 | 3. An application to register in the District Court — ( a )
-- src:6806 | any direction made by the Commission under section 48H(2), 48I or 48L(4), including any direction varied by the Commission under section 48N(6)( b )(i) (called in this Order a Direction);
-- src:6807 | ( b )
-- src:6808 | any written notice by the Commission (called in this Order a Notice) for the payment of any sum comprising — (i)
-- src:6809 | a financial penalty imposed under section 48J(1), including a financial penalty varied by the Commission under section 48N(6)( b )(ii); and
-- src:6810 | (ii)
-- src:6811 | any interest payable under section 48K(10) on that financial penalty; or
-- src:6812 | ( c )
-- src:6813 | any direction or decision made by an Appeal Committee under section 48Q(5) (called in this Order a Decision),
-- src:6814 | must be made by originating application without notice.
@ref O 57 r 3 (src:6805-6814)
GIVEN instrument IS A `o 57 r 3 instrument`
      `the application is made by originating application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made without notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 3 the application to register is made in the way the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`o 57 r 3 the instrument is a Direction, a Notice or a Decision` instrument)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 3 speaks of an application to register a Direction, a Notice or a Decision
        IF `the application is made by originating application` AND `the application is made without notice`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be made by originating application without notice"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4) says what the Court may do about non-compliance) / other: JUST FALSE

-- The Rule opens "An application to register in the District Court", so the court matters: an application to register in another court is
-- outside the sentence, and a scope limit with no "only" says nothing of it (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c)).  This function adds the court as an input and
-- hands the rest to the function above, which is kept as it was.
-- src:6805 | 3. An application to register in the District Court — ( a )
@ref O 57 r 3 (src:6805)
GIVEN `the application is to register in the District Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      instrument IS A `o 57 r 3 instrument`
      `the application is made by originating application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made without notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 3 the application to register in the District Court is made in the way the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the application is to register in the District Court`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 3 speaks of "An application to register in the District Court", and a scope limit with no "only" says nothing of an application to register in another court
    ELSE `o 57 r 3 the application to register is made in the way the Rule requires` instrument `the application is made by originating application` `the application is made without notice`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 4 -- evidence in support of the application to register`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- What the supporting affidavit contains, item by item (rule 4(1)).  Item (d)(ii) is met by (A) or (B);
-- item (d)(iv) is required "if applicable", that is, where a financial penalty was imposed.
DECLARE `o 57 r 4(1) affidavit` HAS
    `o 57 r 4(1)(a) exhibits the instrument or a verified or certified or otherwise duly authenticated copy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 57 r 4(1)(b) states that the Commission is the party seeking to register it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 57 r 4(1)(c) states the name and the usual or last known place of business or residence of the party against whom it has been made, so far as known` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 57 r 4(1)(d)(i) states that the Commission is entitled to enforce it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 57 r 4(1)(d)(ii)(A) states that it has not been appealed against and the time allowed for appealing has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 57 r 4(1)(d)(ii)(B) states that all appeals have been finally disposed of and no further appeal is feasible` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 57 r 4(1)(d)(iii) states that it has not been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 57 r 4(1)(d)(iv) a financial penalty was imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 57 r 4(1)(d)(iv) states the amount of the financial penalty that remains unsatisfied` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:6816 | 4. —(1) An application under section 48M to register in the District Court a Direction, Notice or Decision must be supported by an affidavit — ( a )
-- src:6817 | exhibiting the Direction, Notice or Decision sought to be registered or a verified or certified or otherwise duly authenticated copy of the Direction, Notice or Decision;
-- src:6818 | ( b )
-- src:6819 | stating that the Commission is the party seeking to register the Direction, Notice or Decision;
-- src:6820 | ( c )
-- src:6821 | stating the name and the usual or last known place of business or residence of the party against whom the Direction, Notice or Decision has been made so far as known to the deponent; and
-- src:6822 | ( d )
-- src:6823 | stating to the best of the information or belief of the deponent that — (i)
-- src:6824 | the Commission is entitled to enforce the Direction, Notice or Decision;
-- src:6825 | (ii)
-- src:6826 | as at the date of the application — (A)
-- src:6827 | the Direction, Notice or Decision has not been appealed against and the time allowed for appealing has expired; or
-- src:6828 | (B)
-- src:6829 | all appeals against the Direction, Notice or Decision under section 48Q(1)( a ) or ( b ) or section 48R(1) or (4) have been finally disposed of and no further appeal is feasible;
-- src:6830 | (iii)
-- src:6831 | as at the date of the application, the Direction, Notice or Decision has not been complied with; and
-- src:6832 | (iv)
-- src:6833 | the amount of financial penalty imposed thereunder which remains unsatisfied, if applicable.
@ref O 57 r 4(1) (src:6816-6833)
GIVEN affidavit IS A `o 57 r 4(1) affidavit`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`o 57 r 4(1) the matters the affidavit has not yet stated` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (IF affidavit's `o 57 r 4(1)(a) exhibits the instrument or a verified or certified or otherwise duly authenticated copy` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(a) exhibiting the Direction, Notice or Decision sought to be registered or a verified or certified or otherwise duly authenticated copy"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 57 r 4(1)(b) states that the Commission is the party seeking to register it` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(b) stating that the Commission is the party seeking to register the Direction, Notice or Decision"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 57 r 4(1)(c) states the name and the usual or last known place of business or residence of the party against whom it has been made, so far as known` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(c) stating the name and the usual or last known place of business or residence of the party against whom the Direction, Notice or Decision has been made"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 57 r 4(1)(d)(i) states that the Commission is entitled to enforce it` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(d)(i) the Commission is entitled to enforce the Direction, Notice or Decision"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 57 r 4(1)(d)(ii)(A) states that it has not been appealed against and the time allowed for appealing has expired` OR affidavit's `o 57 r 4(1)(d)(ii)(B) states that all appeals have been finally disposed of and no further appeal is feasible` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(d)(ii) as at the date of the application, either (A) not appealed against and the time allowed for appealing has expired, or (B) all appeals finally disposed of and no further appeal is feasible"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 57 r 4(1)(d)(iii) states that it has not been complied with` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(d)(iii) as at the date of the application, the Direction, Notice or Decision has not been complied with"),
        (IF (NOT (affidavit's `o 57 r 4(1)(d)(iv) a financial penalty was imposed`)) OR affidavit's `o 57 r 4(1)(d)(iv) states the amount of the financial penalty that remains unsatisfied` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(d)(iv) the amount of financial penalty imposed thereunder which remains unsatisfied"))

-- src:6816 | 4. —(1) An application under section 48M to register in the District Court a Direction, Notice or Decision must be supported by an affidavit — ( a )
-- src:6817 | exhibiting the Direction, Notice or Decision sought to be registered or a verified or certified or otherwise duly authenticated copy of the Direction, Notice or Decision;
-- src:6818 | ( b )
-- src:6819 | stating that the Commission is the party seeking to register the Direction, Notice or Decision;
-- src:6820 | ( c )
-- src:6821 | stating the name and the usual or last known place of business or residence of the party against whom the Direction, Notice or Decision has been made so far as known to the deponent; and
-- src:6822 | ( d )
-- src:6823 | stating to the best of the information or belief of the deponent that — (i)
-- src:6824 | the Commission is entitled to enforce the Direction, Notice or Decision;
-- src:6825 | (ii)
-- src:6826 | as at the date of the application — (A)
-- src:6827 | the Direction, Notice or Decision has not been appealed against and the time allowed for appealing has expired; or
-- src:6828 | (B)
-- src:6829 | all appeals against the Direction, Notice or Decision under section 48Q(1)( a ) or ( b ) or section 48R(1) or (4) have been finally disposed of and no further appeal is feasible;
-- src:6830 | (iii)
-- src:6831 | as at the date of the application, the Direction, Notice or Decision has not been complied with; and
-- src:6832 | (iv)
-- src:6833 | the amount of financial penalty imposed thereunder which remains unsatisfied, if applicable.
@ref O 57 r 4(1) (src:6816-6833)
GIVEN affidavit IS A `o 57 r 4(1) affidavit`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 4(1) the affidavit supporting the application states what the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF count (`o 57 r 4(1) the matters the affidavit has not yet stated` affidavit) EQUALS 0
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be supported by an affidavit"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4) says what the Court may do about non-compliance) / other: JUST FALSE

-- Rule 4(2): "In addition", for a Direction or a Notice (not a Decision).
DECLARE `o 57 r 4(2) additional statements` HAS
    `o 57 r 4(2)(a) states that no application to reconsider was made under section 48N(1) and the time allowed to apply has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 57 r 4(2)(b)(i) states that all applications to reconsider have been finally disposed of and the decision on reconsideration has not been appealed against and the time allowed for appealing has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 57 r 4(2)(b)(ii) states that all applications to reconsider have been finally disposed of and all appeals against the decision on reconsideration have been finally disposed of and the time allowed for a further appeal has expired` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:6834 | (2) In addition, an affidavit supporting an application to register in the District Court a Direction or Notice must state that at the date of the application — ( a )
@ref O 57 r 4(2) (src:6834)
GIVEN instrument IS A `o 57 r 3 instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 4(2) the additional statement is required` MEANS
    IF    `o 57 r 3(a) the instrument is a Direction` instrument EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `o 57 r 3(b) the instrument is a Notice` instrument EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 4(2) speaks of "an application to register in the District Court a Direction or Notice", and a scope limit with no "only" says nothing of a Decision

-- src:6834 | (2) In addition, an affidavit supporting an application to register in the District Court a Direction or Notice must state that at the date of the application — ( a )
-- src:6835 | there has been no application made under section 48N(1) to the Commission to reconsider the Direction or Notice and the time allowed to apply for reconsideration has expired; or
-- src:6836 | ( b )
-- src:6837 | all applications made under section 48N(1) to the Commission to reconsider the Direction or Notice have been finally disposed of and — (i)
-- src:6838 | the decision of the Commission made under section 48N(6)( b ) upon reconsideration of the Direction or Notice has not been appealed against and the time allowed for appealing has expired; or
-- src:6839 | (ii)
-- src:6840 | all appeals against the decision of the Commission made under section 48N(6)( b ) upon reconsideration of the Direction or Notice have been finally disposed of and the time allowed for making a further appeal (where applicable) under section 48Q(1)( c ) or section 48R(1) or (4) has expired.
@ref O 57 r 4(2) (src:6834-6840)
GIVEN instrument IS A `o 57 r 3 instrument`
      additional IS A `o 57 r 4(2) additional statements`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 4(2) the affidavit makes the additional statement the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`o 57 r 4(2) the additional statement is required` instrument EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the additional statement is required for a Direction or a Notice; QD: NOTHING, and the companion `o 57 r 4(2) the additional statement is required` says whether it arises / other: JUST TRUE (nothing is unmet)
        IF    additional's `o 57 r 4(2)(a) states that no application to reconsider was made under section 48N(1) and the time allowed to apply has expired`
           OR additional's `o 57 r 4(2)(b)(i) states that all applications to reconsider have been finally disposed of and the decision on reconsideration has not been appealed against and the time allowed for appealing has expired`
           OR additional's `o 57 r 4(2)(b)(ii) states that all applications to reconsider have been finally disposed of and all appeals against the decision on reconsideration have been finally disposed of and the time allowed for a further appeal has expired`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must state"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Whether each statement MAY be made on the facts.  The functions above ask what the affidavit says; these ask whether the facts allow
-- the statement the Rule requires.  The Rule makes each statement "to the best of the information or belief of the deponent", so the
-- facts are the facts as the deponent believes them.  Each statement is the clause's own condition ("has not been appealed against and the
-- time allowed for appealing has expired"): when the facts do not meet it the statement cannot be made, and the clause says so in its own
-- words (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b), a condition the text states and the facts do not meet: JUST FALSE).  What follows if an affidavit
-- states something untrue is not in the Rule (O 3 r 2(4) says what the Court may do about non-compliance).
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (d)(ii)(A): "the Direction, Notice or Decision has not been appealed against and the time allowed for appealing has expired".
-- src:6826 | as at the date of the application — (A)
-- src:6827 | the Direction, Notice or Decision has not been appealed against and the time allowed for appealing has expired; or
@ref O 57 r 4(1) (src:6826-6827)
GIVEN `the Direction, Notice or Decision has been appealed against` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time allowed for appealing has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 4(1)(d)(ii)(A) the affidavit may state that it has not been appealed against and the time allowed for appealing has expired` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the Direction, Notice or Decision has been appealed against`)) AND `the time allowed for appealing has expired`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Direction, Notice or Decision has not been appealed against and the time allowed for appealing has expired"

-- (d)(ii)(B): "all appeals ... have been finally disposed of and no further appeal is feasible".
