      `a further appeal is feasible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 4(1)(d)(ii)(B) the affidavit may state that all appeals have been finally disposed of and no further appeal is feasible` MEANS
    IF `every appeal against the Direction, Notice or Decision has been finally disposed of` AND (NOT (`a further appeal is feasible`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "have been finally disposed of and no further appeal is feasible"

-- (d)(ii) as a whole: "as at the date of the application", route (A) or route (B).
-- src:6825 | (ii)
-- src:6826 | as at the date of the application — (A)
-- src:6827 | the Direction, Notice or Decision has not been appealed against and the time allowed for appealing has expired; or
-- src:6828 | (B)
