@ref O 57 r 4(1) (src:6825-6829)
GIVEN `the Direction, Notice or Decision has been appealed against` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time allowed for appealing has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every appeal against the Direction, Notice or Decision has been finally disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a further appeal is feasible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 4(1)(d)(ii) the affidavit may state the matter the Rule requires about appeals` MEANS
    IF    `o 57 r 4(1)(d)(ii)(A) the affidavit may state that it has not been appealed against and the time allowed for appealing has expired` `the Direction, Notice or Decision has been appealed against` `the time allowed for appealing has expired` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `o 57 r 4(1)(d)(ii)(B) the affidavit may state that all appeals have been finally disposed of and no further appeal is feasible` `every appeal against the Direction, Notice or Decision has been finally disposed of` `a further appeal is feasible` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as at the date of the application"

