-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 5 -- order for registration`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- S-P1: the Form number is a STRING constant.  The form itself is not encoded (inert: a form).
`o 57 r 5(1) the form of the order for registration` MEANS "86"

-- src:6842 | 5. —(1) An order in Form 86 to register a Direction, Notice or Decision must be drawn up by, or on behalf of, the Commission and served on the party against whom the Direction, Notice or Decision has been made. (2) Unless the Court otherwise directs, every order registering a Direction, Notice or Decision must state the period within which an application may be made to set aside the registration of the Direction, Notice or Decision, and must contain a notification that an enforcement order to enforce the Direction, Notice or Decision will not be issued until after the expiry of that period.
@ref O 57 r 5(1) (src:6842)
GIVEN `the order is in Form 86` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is drawn up by or on behalf of the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is served on the party against whom the Direction, Notice or Decision has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 5(1) the order for registration is drawn up and served as the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF `the order is in Form 86` AND `the order is drawn up by or on behalf of the Commission` AND `the order is served on the party against whom the Direction, Notice or Decision has been made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be drawn up by, or on behalf of, the Commission and served"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- "Unless the Court otherwise directs, every order registering ... must state the period ... and must contain a notification".
