    IF `the Court otherwise directs`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the Court otherwise directs"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:6842 | 5. —(1) An order in Form 86 to register a Direction, Notice or Decision must be drawn up by, or on behalf of, the Commission and served on the party against whom the Direction, Notice or Decision has been made. (2) Unless the Court otherwise directs, every order registering a Direction, Notice or Decision must state the period within which an application may be made to set aside the registration of the Direction, Notice or Decision, and must contain a notification that an enforcement order to enforce the Direction, Notice or Decision will not be issued until after the expiry of that period.
