-- src:6848 | 7. —(1) Notice of the registration of a Direction, Notice or Decision must be served on the party against whom the Direction, Notice or Decision has been made and subject to paragraph (2), must be served personally, unless the Court otherwise orders. (2) Service of such a notice out of Singapore is permissible without permission, and Order 8, Rules 2, 3, 7 and 8 apply in relation to such a notice as they apply in relation to an originating claim.
@ref O 57 r 7(1) (src:6848)
GIVEN `the notice is served on the party against whom the Direction, Notice or Decision has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is served personally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has ordered that it be served otherwise than personally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is served in the way the Court ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is served out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 7(1) the notice of registration is served as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the notice is served out of Singapore`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): personal service is "subject to paragraph (2)", and paragraph (2) applies Order 8, Rules 2, 3, 7 and 8, which are in another part
        IF `the notice is served on the party against whom the Direction, Notice or Decision has been made` AND (`the notice is served personally` OR (`the Court has ordered that it be served otherwise than personally` AND `it is served in the way the Court ordered`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be served ... personally, unless the Court otherwise orders"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

