-- src:6856 | the period within which an application to set aside the registration may be made.
@ref O 57 r 7(3) (src:6849-6856)
GIVEN notice IS A `o 57 r 7(3) notice of registration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 7(3) the notice of registration states what the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF count (`o 57 r 7(3) the matters the notice has not yet stated` notice) EQUALS 0
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must state"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 8 -- endorsement of service`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration": the period, counted by O 3 r 3.
-- src:6858 | 8. —(1) Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration or within such longer period as the Court may, in special circumstances, allow, the notice or a copy of the notice must be endorsed by the person who served it with the day of the week and date on which it was served. (2) If the notice is not so endorsed within the period mentioned in paragraph (1), the person seeking to enforce the Direction, Notice or Decision to which the notice relates may not apply for an enforcement order to enforce the Direction, Notice or Decision without the permission of the Court.
@ref O 57 r 8(1) (src:6858)
`o 57 r 8(1) the period for endorsing the notice` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 3
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- The 3 days run to the last day that O 3 r 3 counts (O 3 r 3(3): the period begins immediately after the
-- date of service; r 3(6): being 6 days or less it excludes non-court days).  The Court may allow a longer
-- period "in special circumstances"; its last day, if it has allowed one, replaces the 3-day last day when
-- later.
GIVEN `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the longer period the Court has allowed in special circumstances, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`o 57 r 8(1) the last day for endorsing the notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the longer period the Court has allowed in special circumstances, if it has`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
    WHEN JUST longer THEN IF longer AT LEAST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` THEN longer ELSE `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`

-- src:6858 | 8. —(1) Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration or within such longer period as the Court may, in special circumstances, allow, the notice or a copy of the notice must be endorsed by the person who served it with the day of the week and date on which it was served. (2) If the notice is not so endorsed within the period mentioned in paragraph (1), the person seeking to enforce the Direction, Notice or Decision to which the notice relates may not apply for an enforcement order to enforce the Direction, Notice or Decision without the permission of the Court.
@ref O 57 r 8(1) (src:6858)
GIVEN `the date the notice was endorsed, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date being asked about` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the longer period the Court has allowed in special circumstances, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 8(1) the notice is endorsed in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the notice was endorsed, if it was`
    WHEN JUST endorsed THEN
        IF endorsed AT MOST `o 57 r 8(1) the last day for endorsing the notice` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` `the last day of the longer period the Court has allowed in special circumstances, if it has`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration or within such longer period as the Court may, in special circumstances, allow"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the date being asked about` AT MOST `o 57 r 8(1) the last day for endorsing the notice` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` `the last day of the longer period the Court has allowed in special circumstances, if it has`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the notice is not yet endorsed and the time for endorsing it has not yet run out
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration or within such longer period as the Court may, in special circumstances, allow"

-- src:6858 | 8. —(1) Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration or within such longer period as the Court may, in special circumstances, allow, the notice or a copy of the notice must be endorsed by the person who served it with the day of the week and date on which it was served. (2) If the notice is not so endorsed within the period mentioned in paragraph (1), the person seeking to enforce the Direction, Notice or Decision to which the notice relates may not apply for an enforcement order to enforce the Direction, Notice or Decision without the permission of the Court.
@ref O 57 r 8(1) (src:6858)
GIVEN `there are special circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 8(1) the Court may allow a longer period for endorsing the notice` MEANS
    IF `there are special circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Court may allow a longer period "in special circumstances" and the paragraph says nothing of other cases

DECLARE `o 57 r 8(1) endorsement` HAS
    `o 57 r 8(1) made by the person who served the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 57 r 8(1) states the day of the week on which it was served` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 57 r 8(1) states the date on which it was served` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:6858 | 8. —(1) Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration or within such longer period as the Court may, in special circumstances, allow, the notice or a copy of the notice must be endorsed by the person who served it with the day of the week and date on which it was served. (2) If the notice is not so endorsed within the period mentioned in paragraph (1), the person seeking to enforce the Direction, Notice or Decision to which the notice relates may not apply for an enforcement order to enforce the Direction, Notice or Decision without the permission of the Court.
@ref O 57 r 8(1) (src:6858)
GIVEN endorsement IS A `o 57 r 8(1) endorsement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 8(1) the endorsement is what the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF    endorsement's `o 57 r 8(1) made by the person who served the notice`
      AND endorsement's `o 57 r 8(1) states the day of the week on which it was served`
      AND endorsement's `o 57 r 8(1) states the date on which it was served`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be endorsed by the person who served it with the day of the week and date"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- The duty as a regulative rule: the person who served the notice (named in the text) must endorse it.
-- The time unit of the trace is a day counted as O 3 r 3 counts it.  The longer period the Court may allow
-- is not modelled in the rule (it is in `o 57 r 8(1) the notice is endorsed in time`).
DECLARE `o 57 r 8(1) party` IS ONE OF
    `o 57 r 8(1) the person who served the notice`

DECLARE `o 57 r 8(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `o 57 r 8(1) endorse the notice with the day of the week and date of service`

`o 57 r 8(1) the duty to endorse the notice` MEANS
    PARTY `o 57 r 8(1) the person who served the notice`
    MUST `o 57 r 8(1) endorse the notice with the day of the week and date of service`
    WITHIN 3
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 57 r 8(1) the person who served the notice` BECAUSE "the notice was not endorsed within 3 days after its service (O 57 r 8(1))"

-- Endorsed on day 2: fulfilled.
#TRACE `o 57 r 8(1) the duty to endorse the notice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 57 r 8(1) the person who served the notice` DOES `o 57 r 8(1) endorse the notice with the day of the week and date of service` AT 2
-- Endorsed on day 3, the last day: fulfilled.
#TRACE `o 57 r 8(1) the duty to endorse the notice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 57 r 8(1) the person who served the notice` DOES `o 57 r 8(1) endorse the notice with the day of the week and date of service` AT 3
-- Not endorsed by day 4: breach.
#TRACE `o 57 r 8(1) the duty to endorse the notice` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 4

-- "(2) If the notice is not so endorsed within the period mentioned in paragraph (1), the person seeking to
-- enforce ... may not apply for an enforcement order ... without the permission of the Court."
-- src:6858 | 8. —(1) Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration or within such longer period as the Court may, in special circumstances, allow, the notice or a copy of the notice must be endorsed by the person who served it with the day of the week and date on which it was served. (2) If the notice is not so endorsed within the period mentioned in paragraph (1), the person seeking to enforce the Direction, Notice or Decision to which the notice relates may not apply for an enforcement order to enforce the Direction, Notice or Decision without the permission of the Court.
@ref O 57 r 8(2) (src:6858)
GIVEN `the answer on whether the notice was endorsed in time` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 8(2) the person seeking to enforce may apply for an enforcement order without the permission of the Court` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer on whether the notice was endorsed in time`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not apply for an enforcement order to enforce the Direction, Notice or Decision without the permission of the Court"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar of paragraph (2) does not arise, and a bar that does not arise grants no permission; QA: NOTHING (a lifted bar grants nothing) / other: JUST TRUE (the exception permits it)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the notice was endorsed in time is not yet answered

-- src:6859 | (3) Every affidavit of service of any such notice must state the date on which the notice was endorsed under this Rule.
@ref O 57 r 8(3) (src:6859)
GIVEN `the affidavit of service states the date on which the notice was endorsed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 8(3) the affidavit of service states the date of endorsement` MEANS
    IF `the affidavit of service states the date on which the notice was endorsed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "Every affidavit of service of any such notice must state the date"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 9 -- application to set aside registration`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6861 | 9. —(1) An application to set aside the registration of a Direction, Notice or Decision must be made by summons supported by an affidavit. (2) The Court hearing such application may order any issue between — ( a )
@ref O 57 r 9(1) (src:6861)
GIVEN document IS A `Document kind`
      `the application is supported by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 9(1) the application to set aside the registration is made as the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF document EQUALS Summons AND `the application is supported by an affidavit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be made by summons supported by an affidavit"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- src:6861 | 9. —(1) An application to set aside the registration of a Direction, Notice or Decision must be made by summons supported by an affidavit. (2) The Court hearing such application may order any issue between — ( a )
-- src:6862 | the Commission and the party against whom the Direction, Notice or Decision is made; or
-- src:6863 | ( b )
-- src:6864 | the complainant referred to in section 48H(1) upon whose application a Direction, Notice or Decision is made and the party against whom the Direction, Notice or Decision is made,
-- src:6865 | to be tried in any manner in which an issue in an action may be ordered to be tried.
@ref O 57 r 9(2) (src:6861-6865)
GIVEN `the issue is between the Commission and the party against whom the Direction, Notice or Decision is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issue is between the complainant referred to in section 48H(1) upon whose application the Direction, Notice or Decision is made and the party against whom it is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 9(2) the Court may order the issue to be tried as an issue in an action is tried` MEANS
    IF `the issue is between the Commission and the party against whom the Direction, Notice or Decision is made` OR `the issue is between the complainant referred to in section 48H(1) upon whose application the Direction, Notice or Decision is made and the party against whom it is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power names an issue between two pairs of parties and says nothing of any other issue

-- src:6866 | (3) The Court hearing an application under this Rule to set aside the registration of a Direction, Notice or Decision may order the registration of the Direction, Notice or Decision to be set aside on such terms as the Court thinks fit.
@ref O 57 r 9(3) (src:6866)
GIVEN `the Court is hearing an application under this Rule to set aside the registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 9(3) the Court may order the registration to be set aside on such terms as it thinks fit` MEANS
    IF `the Court is hearing an application under this Rule to set aside the registration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given to "The Court hearing an application under this Rule"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 10 -- issue of enforcement order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "(1) Where, pursuant to Rule 5(2), there is a specified period ..., an enforcement order must not be issued
-- ... until after the expiry of the specified period, or if that period has been extended by the Court, until
-- after the expiry of that period so extended."  The "until" bar is its own yes/no (ruling of 2026-11-05 (d)):
-- JUST TRUE before the expiry, JUST FALSE after it.  Nothing here says the order MAY be issued after it.
-- src:6868 | 10. —(1) Where, pursuant to Rule 5(2), there is a specified period within which an application may be made to set aside the registration of a Direction, Notice or Decision, an enforcement order must not be issued to enforce the Direction, Notice or Decision until after the expiry of the specified period, or if that period has been extended by the Court, until after the expiry of that period so extended. (2) If an application is made to set aside the registration of a Direction, Notice or Decision, an enforcement order to enforce the Direction, Notice or Decision must not be issued until after such application is disposed of.
@ref O 57 r 10(1) (src:6868)
GIVEN `there is a specified period under Rule 5(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the specified period expires, as extended by the Court if it was` IS A DATE
      `the date being asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 10(1) an enforcement order cannot yet be issued because the specified period has not expired` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`there is a specified period under Rule 5(2)`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, pursuant to Rule 5(2), there is a specified period within which an application may be made to set aside the registration"
        IF `the date being asked about` AT MOST `the date the specified period expires, as extended by the Court if it was`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until after the expiry of the specified period"

-- "(2) If an application is made to set aside the registration ..., an enforcement order ... must not be
-- issued until after such application is disposed of."
-- src:6868 | 10. —(1) Where, pursuant to Rule 5(2), there is a specified period within which an application may be made to set aside the registration of a Direction, Notice or Decision, an enforcement order must not be issued to enforce the Direction, Notice or Decision until after the expiry of the specified period, or if that period has been extended by the Court, until after the expiry of that period so extended. (2) If an application is made to set aside the registration of a Direction, Notice or Decision, an enforcement order to enforce the Direction, Notice or Decision must not be issued until after such application is disposed of.
@ref O 57 r 10(2) (src:6868)
GIVEN `an application is made to set aside the registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that application has been disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 10(2) an enforcement order cannot yet be issued because the application to set aside is not disposed of` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`an application is made to set aside the registration`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an application is made to set aside the registration"
        IF NOT (`that application has been disposed of`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until after such application is disposed of"

-- src:6869 | (3) Any party wishing to apply for an enforcement order to enforce a Direction, Notice or Decision registered in accordance with this Order must produce to the Court an affidavit of service of the notice of registration of the Direction, Notice or Decision and any order made by the Court in relation to the Direction, Notice or Decision.
@ref O 57 r 10(3) (src:6869)
GIVEN `the party produces to the Court an affidavit of service of the notice of registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an order made by the Court in relation to the Direction, Notice or Decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party produces that order to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 10(3) the party applying for an enforcement order has produced what the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF `the party produces to the Court an affidavit of service of the notice of registration` AND ((NOT (`there is an order made by the Court in relation to the Direction, Notice or Decision`)) OR `the party produces that order to the Court`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must produce to the Court an affidavit of service ... and any order made by the Court"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- The two "until" bars as prohibitions on a trace.  The text names no one who bears them ("an enforcement
-- order must not be issued"), so the party below is a PLACEHOLDER for whoever issues the order, not an
-- actor the text names; no seat is written for it.  The trace's time unit is a day, counted from the day
-- asked about to the day the specified period expires.
DECLARE `o 57 r 10 party` IS ONE OF
    `o 57 r 10 whoever issues the enforcement order`

DECLARE `o 57 r 10 act` IS ONE OF
    `o 57 r 10 issue the enforcement order`

GIVEN `days from the day asked about to the day the specified period expires` IS A NUMBER
`o 57 r 10(1) the prohibition on issuing the enforcement order` MEANS
    PARTY `o 57 r 10 whoever issues the enforcement order`
    SHANT `o 57 r 10 issue the enforcement order`
    WITHIN `days from the day asked about to the day the specified period expires`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 57 r 10 whoever issues the enforcement order` BECAUSE "an enforcement order was issued before the expiry of the specified period (O 57 r 10(1))"

-- Ten days to run: an order issued on day 4 breaches the prohibition; none issued by day 11 fulfils it.
#TRACE `o 57 r 10(1) the prohibition on issuing the enforcement order` 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 57 r 10 whoever issues the enforcement order` DOES `o 57 r 10 issue the enforcement order` AT 4
#TRACE `o 57 r 10(1) the prohibition on issuing the enforcement order` 10 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 11

GIVEN `days until the application to set aside is disposed of` IS A NUMBER
`o 57 r 10(2) the prohibition on issuing the enforcement order while the application is undisposed` MEANS
    PARTY `o 57 r 10 whoever issues the enforcement order`
    SHANT `o 57 r 10 issue the enforcement order`
    WITHIN `days until the application to set aside is disposed of`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 57 r 10 whoever issues the enforcement order` BECAUSE "an enforcement order was issued before the application to set aside was disposed of (O 57 r 10(2))"

#TRACE `o 57 r 10(2) the prohibition on issuing the enforcement order while the application is undisposed` 6 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 57 r 10 whoever issues the enforcement order` DOES `o 57 r 10 issue the enforcement order` AT 5
#TRACE `o 57 r 10(2) the prohibition on issuing the enforcement order while the application is undisposed` 6 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 7

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 11 -- application for enforcement order under section 48M(4)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 57 r 11(1)(a) when the application is made` IS ONE OF
    `o 57 r 11(1)(a) together with the application for registration`
    `o 57 r 11(1)(a) at a time after the application for registration`
    `o 57 r 11(1)(a) before the application for registration`

-- The text fixes the time in its own words: "together with, or at any time after".  An application made before the application for
-- registration is outside that window, and the answer outside a window the text fixes is JUST FALSE (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)).
-- src:6871 | 11. —(1) An application for any order specified in section 48M(4) in relation to any Direction, Notice or Decision — ( a )
-- src:6872 | may be made together with, or at any time after, an application for registration under Rule 3 relating to that same Direction, Notice or Decision; and
@ref O 57 r 11(1) (src:6871-6872)
GIVEN `when it is made` IS A `o 57 r 11(1)(a) when the application is made`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 11(1)(a) the application for an order specified in section 48M(4) may be made at this time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `when it is made`
    WHEN `o 57 r 11(1)(a) together with the application for registration` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 57 r 11(1)(a) at a time after the application for registration` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 57 r 11(1)(a) before the application for registration` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "together with, or at any time after, an application for registration"

-- src:6873 | ( b )
-- src:6874 | does not constitute an application for an enforcement order to enforce that Direction, Notice or Decision under Rule 10.
@ref O 57 r 11(1) (src:6873-6874)
GIVEN `the application is for an order specified in section 48M(4) in relation to a Direction, Notice or Decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 11(1)(b) the application is an application for an enforcement order under Rule 10` MEANS
    IF `the application is for an order specified in section 48M(4) in relation to a Direction, Notice or Decision`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not constitute an application for an enforcement order"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (1)(b) speaks only of "an application for any order specified in section 48M(4)"

DECLARE `o 57 r 11(2) how the application is made` IS ONE OF
    `o 57 r 11(2) by summons supported by an affidavit, with notice`
    `o 57 r 11(2) by summons supported by an affidavit, without notice`

-- src:6875 | (2) The application referred to in paragraph (1) may be made by summons supported by an affidavit and where the case is one of urgency, may be made without notice.
@ref O 57 r 11(2) (src:6875)
GIVEN how IS A `o 57 r 11(2) how the application is made`
      `the case is one of urgency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 11(2) the application may be made in this way` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `o 57 r 11(2) by summons supported by an affidavit, with notice` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 57 r 11(2) by summons supported by an affidavit, without notice` THEN
        IF `the case is one of urgency`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the case is one of urgency, may be made without notice"

DECLARE `o 57 r 11(3) affidavit` HAS
    `o 57 r 11(3)(a) states the grounds relied upon by the applicant for the order sought` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 57 r 11(3)(b) states the appropriateness of the order sought in addressing the grounds relied upon` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:6876 | (3) The affidavit must state — ( a )
-- src:6877 | the grounds relied upon by the applicant for the order sought; and
-- src:6878 | ( b )
-- src:6879 | the appropriateness of the order sought in addressing the grounds relied upon by the applicant.
@ref O 57 r 11(3) (src:6876-6879)
GIVEN affidavit IS A `o 57 r 11(3) affidavit`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`o 57 r 11(3) the matters the affidavit has not yet stated` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (IF affidavit's `o 57 r 11(3)(a) states the grounds relied upon by the applicant for the order sought` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(a) the grounds relied upon by the applicant for the order sought"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 57 r 11(3)(b) states the appropriateness of the order sought in addressing the grounds relied upon` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(b) the appropriateness of the order sought in addressing the grounds relied upon by the applicant"))

-- src:6876 | (3) The affidavit must state — ( a )
-- src:6877 | the grounds relied upon by the applicant for the order sought; and
-- src:6878 | ( b )
-- src:6879 | the appropriateness of the order sought in addressing the grounds relied upon by the applicant.
@ref O 57 r 11(3) (src:6876-6879)
GIVEN affidavit IS A `o 57 r 11(3) affidavit`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 11(3) the affidavit states what the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF count (`o 57 r 11(3) the matters the affidavit has not yet stated` affidavit) EQUALS 0
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "The affidavit must state"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

