GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 12 the duty to serve a copy on the Commission arises` MEANS
    IF `a claim is made for relief in civil proceedings under section 48O(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any claim is made for relief in civil proceedings under section 48O(1)"

-- src:6881 | 12. Where any claim is made for relief in civil proceedings under section 48O(1), the claimant in those proceedings must serve a copy of the originating claim or originating application to the Commission not later than 14 days after service of the originating claim or originating application on the defendant.
@ref O 57 r 12 (src:6881)
GIVEN `a claim is made for relief in civil proceedings under section 48O(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date a copy of the originating claim or originating application is served on the Commission` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 12 the claimant serves a copy on the Commission in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a claim is made for relief in civil proceedings under section 48O(1)`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty does not arise; QD: NOTHING, and the companion `o 57 r 12 the duty to serve a copy on the Commission arises` answers JUST FALSE / other: JUST TRUE (nothing is unmet)
        IF `the date a copy of the originating claim or originating application is served on the Commission` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than 14 days after service of the originating claim or originating application on the defendant"

DECLARE `o 57 r 12 party` IS ONE OF
    `o 57 r 12 the claimant`

DECLARE `o 57 r 12 act` IS ONE OF
    `o 57 r 12 serve a copy of the originating claim or originating application on the Commission`

-- The trace's time unit is a day counted from the day the originating claim or originating application was
-- served on the defendant, as O 3 r 3 counts days.
`o 57 r 12 the duty to serve the Commission` MEANS
    PARTY `o 57 r 12 the claimant`
    MUST `o 57 r 12 serve a copy of the originating claim or originating application on the Commission`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 57 r 12 the claimant` BECAUSE "a copy was not served on the Commission not later than 14 days after service on the defendant (O 57 r 12)"

#TRACE `o 57 r 12 the duty to serve the Commission` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 57 r 12 the claimant` DOES `o 57 r 12 serve a copy of the originating claim or originating application on the Commission` AT 14
#TRACE `o 57 r 12 the duty to serve the Commission` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 15

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 13 -- transmission to the Commission of a judgment or order under section 48O`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6883 | 13. Any person who is granted any judgment or order by a Court pursuant to section 48O must transmit a copy of the judgment or order to the Commission within 3 days after the date of the judgment or order.
@ref O 57 r 13 (src:6883)
`o 57 r 13 the period for transmitting a copy to the Commission` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 3
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:6883 | 13. Any person who is granted any judgment or order by a Court pursuant to section 48O must transmit a copy of the judgment or order to the Commission within 3 days after the date of the judgment or order.
@ref O 57 r 13 (src:6883)
GIVEN `the person was granted a judgment or order by a Court pursuant to section 48O` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 13 the duty to transmit a copy to the Commission arises` MEANS
    IF `the person was granted a judgment or order by a Court pursuant to section 48O`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any person who is granted any judgment or order by a Court pursuant to section 48O"

-- src:6883 | 13. Any person who is granted any judgment or order by a Court pursuant to section 48O must transmit a copy of the judgment or order to the Commission within 3 days after the date of the judgment or order.
@ref O 57 r 13 (src:6883)
GIVEN `the person was granted a judgment or order by a Court pursuant to section 48O` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date a copy of the judgment or order is transmitted to the Commission` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 57 r 13 the person transmits a copy to the Commission in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person was granted a judgment or order by a Court pursuant to section 48O`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty does not arise; QD: NOTHING, and the companion `o 57 r 13 the duty to transmit a copy to the Commission arises` answers JUST FALSE / other: JUST TRUE (nothing is unmet)
        IF `the date a copy of the judgment or order is transmitted to the Commission` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 3 days after the date of the judgment or order"

DECLARE `o 57 r 13 party` IS ONE OF
    `o 57 r 13 the person granted the judgment or order`

DECLARE `o 57 r 13 act` IS ONE OF
    `o 57 r 13 transmit a copy of the judgment or order to the Commission`

-- The trace's time unit is a day counted from the date of the judgment or order, as O 3 r 3 counts days.
`o 57 r 13 the duty to transmit the judgment or order` MEANS
    PARTY `o 57 r 13 the person granted the judgment or order`
    MUST `o 57 r 13 transmit a copy of the judgment or order to the Commission`
    WITHIN 3
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 57 r 13 the person granted the judgment or order` BECAUSE "a copy was not transmitted to the Commission within 3 days after the date of the judgment or order (O 57 r 13)"

#TRACE `o 57 r 13 the duty to transmit the judgment or order` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 57 r 13 the person granted the judgment or order` DOES `o 57 r 13 transmit a copy of the judgment or order to the Commission` AT 3
#TRACE `o 57 r 13 the duty to transmit the judgment or order` AT 0 WITH
